# Faster Local Cream and Frosted Reading Pane

Status: DONE
Milestone: M26 Visible cream movement behind readable glass
Dependencies: 28_CREAM_TRAILS_LAYOUT_AND_PAPER.todo

## Purpose

The owner wants the local preview blobs to move farther and faster, and remain
visible behind the centered text through a seamlessly blended frosted pane.
Keep this change isolated from the published bakery website.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the previous local experiment and context.
- [x] Replace tiny edge-limited oscillations with larger bounded inward-shifted orbits.
- [x] Increase motion phase speed by2.25while retaining the30fpspaint ceiling.
- [x] Ensure multiple cream forms travel through the central reading area.
- [x] Replace the96%opaque text wash with14%tint and8pxbackdrop frost.
- [x] Keep actual lettering and controls sharp, with soft low-contrast pane edges.
- [x] Preserve reduced-transparency, print, forced-colour and motion fallbacks.
- [x] Retain the small cursor tail, peaks, paper pattern, Pause and scoop limits.
- [x] Verify actual pane transmission and sampled reading contrast with a rendered cream fixture.
- [x] Confirm public site/README/HEAD remain unchanged; no deployment.

## Acceptance criteria

- More visible travel, no clipping at viewport bounds or initial pose jump.
- Cream actually visible through the pane rather than hidden by another opaque card.
- Frost affects the background, not foreground text.
- Pause freezes all motion; inactive and reduced-motion behavior remains safe.
- No image-tool views or unsupported claim of new visual acceptance.

